{"id":"mahabharata-5-142","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":142,"title":"द्विचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 142 · Kunti goes to Karna","summary":{"en":"After Krishna's mission fails, Vidura tells Kunti that war is now certain, and she is filled with anguish at the thought of her sons fighting one another. She resolves to go to Karna and tell him the truth, and finds him at the Ganga, praying with face upturned to the sun.","kn":"ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಕಾರ್ಯ ವಿಫಲವಾದ ಮೇಲೆ ಈಗ ಯುದ್ಧ ಖಚಿತ ಎಂದು ವಿದುರನು ಕುಂತಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತನ್ನ ಮಕ್ಕಳೇ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಹೋರಾಡುವರೆಂಬ ಯೋಚನೆಯಿಂದ ಅವಳು ವೇದನೆಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಕರ್ಣನ ಬಳಿ ಹೋಗಿ ಸತ್ಯ ತಿಳಿಸಲು ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸಿ, ಸೂರ್ಯನತ್ತ ಮುಖವೆತ್ತಿ ಜಪಿಸುತ್ತಿದ್ದ ಅವನನ್ನು ಗಂಗಾತೀರದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"श्रीकृष्ण का प्रयास विफल होने पर विदुर कुन्ती से कहते हैं कि अब युद्ध निश्चित है, और अपने पुत्रों के आपस में लड़ने के विचार से वे व्याकुल हो जाती हैं। वे कर्ण के पास जाकर सत्य बताने का निश्चय करती हैं और उसे गंगा-तट पर सूर्य की ओर मुख उठाए जप करते पाती हैं।","te":"శ్రీకృష్ణుని ప్రయత్నం విఫలమైన తర్వాత ఇప్పుడు యుద్ధం తథ్యమని విదురుడు కుంతికి చెబుతాడు; తన కుమారులే ఒకరితో ఒకరు పోరాడతారనే ఆలోచనతో ఆమె వేదన చెందుతుంది. కర్ణుని దగ్గరకు వెళ్లి సత్యం చెప్పాలని నిశ్చయించి, సూర్యుని వైపు ముఖం ఎత్తి జపిస్తున్న అతనిని గంగాతీరంలో చూస్తుంది.","ta":"ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரின் முயற்சி தோற்றதும் இனிப் போர் உறுதி என்று விதுரர் குந்தியிடம் சொல்ல, தன் மைந்தர்களே ஒருவரோடொருவர் போரிடுவார்கள் என்ற எண்ணத்தால் அவள் வேதனையுறுகிறாள். கர்ணனிடம் சென்று உண்மையைச் சொல்லத் தீர்மானித்து, சூரியனை நோக்கி முகம் உயர்த்தி ஜபிக்கும் அவனைக் கங்கைக் கரையில் காண்கிறாள்.","ml":"കൃഷ്ണന്റെ ദൗത്യം പരാജയപ്പെട്ടശേഷം, യുദ്ധം ഉറപ്പായെന്ന് വിദുരർ കുന്തിയോട് പറയുന്നു; പരസ്പരം പൊരുതുന്ന മക്കളെക്കുറിച്ചുള്ള ചിന്ത അവളെ വേദനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. കർണ്ണനെ കണ്ട് സത്യം പറയാൻ അവൾ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു; സൂര്യന് നേരെ മുഖമുയർത്തി പ്രാർഥിച്ചുകൊണ്ട് ഗംഗാതീരത്ത് നിൽക്കുന്ന അദ്ദേഹത്തെ അവൾ കണ്ടെത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.142; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"कर्णोपनिवादपर्व","titleEn":"Karnopanivada Parva (The secret talks with Karna)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"असिद्धानुनये कृष्णे कुरुभ्यः पाण्डवान्गते ।\nअभिगम्य पृथां क्षत्ता शनैः शोचन्निवाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Krishna's attempt at conciliation failed and he had gone from the Kurus to the Pandavas, Vidura approached Pritha and spoke to her slowly, as though grieving."}},{"n":2,"text":"जानासि मे जीवपुत्रे भावं नित्यमनुग्रहे ।\nक्रोशतो न च गृह्णीते वचनं मे सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Mother of living sons, you know my feeling, my constant wish to help; yet Suyodhana does not accept my words, though I cry out."}},{"n":3,"text":"उपपन्नो ह्यसौ राजा चेदिपाञ्चालकेकयैः ।\nभीमार्जुनाभ्यां कृष्णेन युयुधानयमैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava king is now joined by the Chedis, Panchalas and Kekayas, by Bhima and Arjuna, by Krishna, Yuyudhana and the twins."}},{"n":4,"text":"उपप्लव्ये निविष्टोऽपि धर्ममेव युधिष्ठिरः ।\nकाङ्क्षते ज्ञातिसौहार्दाद्बलवान्दुर्बलो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though camped at Upaplavya, Yudhishthira still seeks only dharma, out of love for his kinsmen, like a strong man behaving as a weak one."}},{"n":5,"text":"राजा तु धृतराष्ट्रोऽयं वयोवृद्धो न शाम्यति ।\nमत्तः पुत्रमदेनैव विधर्मे पथि वर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"But King Dhritarashtra, old in years, finds no peace; drunk with pride in his son, he walks the path of adharma."}},{"n":6,"text":"जयद्रथस्य कर्णस्य तथा दुःशासनस्य च ।\nसौबलस्य च दुर्बुद्ध्या मिथोभेदः प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through the wicked counsel of Jayadratha, Karna, Duhshasana and Shakuni son of Subala, dissension spreads among them."}},{"n":7,"text":"अधर्मेण हि धर्मिष्ठं हृतं वै राज्यमीदृशम् ।\nयेषां तेषामयं धर्मः सानुबन्धो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a kingdom as righteous as this one has been taken by adharma, those who did it will bear the consequences of that wrong, with all that follows."}},{"n":8,"text":"ह्रियमाणे बलाद्धर्मे कुरुभिः को न संज्वरेत् ।\nअसाम्ना केशवे याते समुद्योक्ष्यन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When dharma is being stolen by force, who among the Kurus would not burn with anguish? With Keshava gone without peace, the Pandavas will take up arms."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः कुरूणामनयो भविता वीरनाशनः ।\nचिन्तयन्न लभे निद्रामहःसु च निशासु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Kurus' folly will bring on the death of heroes. As I think of it I get no sleep, by day or by night.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु कुन्ती तद्वाक्यमर्थकामेन भाषितम् ।\nअनिष्टनन्ती दुःखार्ता मनसा विममर्श ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those words spoken by one who wished her good, Kunti, pained and grieving, disliked them, and pondered in her mind."}},{"n":11,"text":"धिगस्त्वर्थं यत्कृतेऽयं महाञ्ज्ञातिवधे क्षयः ।\nवर्त्स्यते सुहृदां ह्येषां युद्धेऽस्मिन्वै पराभवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She thought: \"Curse wealth, for the sake of which this great slaughter of kinsmen and ruin will come, and defeat for these friends in this battle."}},{"n":12,"text":"पाण्डवाश्चेदिपाञ्चाला यादवाश्च समागताः ।\nभारतैर्यदि योत्स्यन्ति किं नु दुःखमतः परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the Pandavas, Chedis, Panchalas and Yadavas, gathered together, fight the Bharatas, what sorrow could be greater than that?"}},{"n":13,"text":"पश्ये दोषं ध्रुवं युद्धे तथा युद्धे पराभवम् ।\nअधनस्य मृतं श्रेयो न हि ज्ञातिक्षये जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see sure fault in war, and in war defeat. For one without wealth, death is better; there is no victory in the destruction of kin."}},{"n":14,"text":"पितामहः शांतनव आचार्यश्च युधां पतिः ।\nकर्णश्च धार्तराष्ट्रार्थं वर्धयन्ति भयं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"The grandfather, Shantanu's son, the teacher Drona, lord of warriors, and Karna, all working for Dhritarashtra's son, increase my fear."}},{"n":15,"text":"नाचार्यः कामवाञ्शिष्यैर्द्रोणो युध्येत जातु चित् ।\nपाण्डवेषु कथं हार्दं कुर्यान्न च पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The teacher Drona, a man of wishes, would never fight his own pupils, and the grandfather would never be harsh toward the Pandavas."}},{"n":16,"text":"अयं त्वेको वृथादृष्टिर्धार्तराष्ट्रस्य दुर्मतेः ।\nमोहानुवर्ती सततं पापो द्वेष्टि च पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Only this one, Karna, with his vain outlook, ever follows the delusion of wicked-minded Dhritarashtra's son, a sinner who hates the Pandavas."}},{"n":17,"text":"महत्यनर्थे निर्बन्धी बलवांश्च विशेषतः ।\nकर्णः सदा पाण्डवानां तन्मे दहति सांप्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, strong and especially stubborn, is always bent on great harm to the Pandavas, and that burns me now."}},{"n":18,"text":"आशंसे त्वद्य कर्णस्य मनोऽहं पाण्डवान्प्रति ।\nप्रसादयितुमासाद्य दर्शयन्ती यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I mean to approach Karna and appease his heart toward the Pandavas, telling him the truth as it is."}},{"n":19,"text":"तोषितो भगवान्यत्र दुर्वासा मे वरं ददौ ।\nआह्वानं देवसंयुक्तं वसन्त्याः पितृवेश्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"When, in my father's house, I pleased the blessed Durvasa, he gave me a boon: a summons joined with the gods."}},{"n":20,"text":"साहमन्तःपुरे राज्ञः कुन्तिभोजपुरस्कृता ।\nचिन्तयन्ती बहुविधं हृदयेन विदूयता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored in the women's quarters of King Kuntibhoja, with an aching heart I thought in many ways"}},{"n":21,"text":"बलाबलं च मन्त्राणां ब्राह्मणस्य च वाग्बलम् ।\nस्त्रीभावाद्बालभावाच्च चिन्तयन्ती पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"about the strength and weakness of mantras and the power of a brahmin's word, thinking again and again, in the manner of a woman and a girl."}},{"n":22,"text":"धात्र्या विश्रब्धया गुप्ता सखीजनवृता तदा ।\nदोषं परिहरन्ती च पितुश्चारित्ररक्षिणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Guarded then by a trusted nurse and surrounded by my friends, trying to avoid blame and protect my father's name,"}},{"n":23,"text":"कथं नु सुकृतं मे स्यान्नापराधवती कथम् ।\nभवेयमिति संचिन्त्य ब्राह्मणं तं नमस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wondered how I could do good and not be at fault; and after bowing to that brahmin,"}},{"n":24,"text":"कौतूहलात्तु तं लब्ध्वा बालिश्यादाचरं तदा ।\nकन्या सती देवमर्कमासादयमहं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"in curiosity and childishness I then acted, though a maiden, and approached the sun god."}},{"n":25,"text":"योऽसौ कानीनगर्भो मे पुत्रवत्परिवर्तितः ।\nकस्मान्न कुर्याद्वचनं पथ्यं भ्रातृहितं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why should that son, conceived by me as a maiden and raised like a son, not do the good that is in the interest of his brothers?\""}},{"n":26,"text":"इति कुन्ती विनिश्चित्य कार्यं निश्चितमुत्तमम् ।\nकार्यार्थमभिनिर्याय ययौ भागीरथीं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So Kunti decided and, settling on the best course, set out for her purpose and went toward the Bhagirathi."}},{"n":27,"text":"आत्मजस्य ततस्तस्य घृणिनः सत्यसङ्गिनः ।\nगङ्गातीरे पृथाशृण्वदुपाध्ययननिस्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There on the Ganga bank Pritha heard the sound of the Vedic recitation of her merciful, truthful son."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्राङ्मुखस्योर्ध्वबाहोः सा पर्यतिष्ठत पृष्ठतः ।\nजप्यावसानं कार्यार्थं प्रतीक्षन्ती तपस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"He faced east with arms raised, and she stood behind him, the ascetic woman waiting for the end of his prayers, for her purpose."}},{"n":29,"text":"अतिष्ठत्सूर्यतापार्ता कर्णस्योत्तरवाससि ।\nकौरव्यपत्नी वार्ष्णेयी पद्ममालेव शुष्यती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Distressed by the sun's heat, she stood in the shade of Karna's upper garment, the Kuru's wife, the Vrishni woman, withering like a lotus garland."}},{"n":30,"text":"आ पृष्ठतापाज्जप्त्वा स परिवृत्य यतव्रतः ।\nदृष्ट्वा कुन्तीमुपातिष्ठदभिवाद्य कृताञ्जलिः ।\nयथान्यायं महातेजा मानी धर्मभृतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After reciting until his back was scorched by the sun, he of strict vows turned around, saw Kunti, and, proud and mighty, the best of those who uphold dharma, greeted her with joined hands, as is proper."}}]}]}